{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00574",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.63,
      "end_seconds": 10.43,
      "duration_seconds": 9.8,
      "text": "Come in, have a seat. Before we start, how would you like me to address you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.12,
      "end_seconds": 18.8,
      "duration_seconds": 6.68,
      "text": "Oh, Priya is fine. Everyone calls me that. Mrs Nair feels like my mother-in-law."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.33,
      "end_seconds": 31.64,
      "duration_seconds": 11.31,
      "text": "Priya it is. I see you're here for your multiple sclerosis review. How have things been since we last met?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.46,
      "end_seconds": 41.65,
      "duration_seconds": 8.19,
      "text": "Mostly stable, I think. But I'm worried, doctor, because I'm just so tired all the time now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.26,
      "end_seconds": 51.93,
      "duration_seconds": 7.67,
      "text": "Tell me more about the tiredness. Is it sleepiness, or more a heavy, drained feeling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.95,
      "end_seconds": 62.46,
      "duration_seconds": 8.51,
      "text": "Drained. I wake up after eight hours and still feel like I've run a marathon."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.41,
      "end_seconds": 69.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "And when did you first notice the fatigue? Roughly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.57,
      "end_seconds": 83.72,
      "duration_seconds": 12.15,
      "text": "Um, that's the thing, I can't say. Maybe around Christmas, or was it before the summer? I honestly don't know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.74,
      "end_seconds": 94.49,
      "duration_seconds": 9.75,
      "text": "That's fine, it often creeps in slowly. Does it get worse at certain times of day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.72,
      "end_seconds": 106.48,
      "duration_seconds": 9.76,
      "text": "Afternoons are the worst. Is this a relapse? Is the MS getting worse? I keep lying awake thinking about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.8,
      "end_seconds": 118.32,
      "duration_seconds": 10.52,
      "text": "Good question, and I'll come back to it. First, any new numbness, tingling or weakness in your arms or legs?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.26,
      "end_seconds": 127.5,
      "duration_seconds": 6.24,
      "text": "No, nothing new. My legs feel the same as always."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.57,
      "end_seconds": 137.73,
      "duration_seconds": 8.16,
      "text": "Any change in your eyesight, like blurring or pain when you move your eyes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.23,
      "end_seconds": 145.48,
      "duration_seconds": 6.25,
      "text": "No, my eyes have been fine. I'd have rushed in if they weren't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.06,
      "end_seconds": 155.05,
      "duration_seconds": 6.99,
      "text": "Good. Now, let me check your medicines. What are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.46,
      "end_seconds": 167.91,
      "duration_seconds": 11.45,
      "text": "The levothyroxine, 75 micrograms, every morning on an empty stomach. And a vitamin D, 1000 units once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.72,
      "end_seconds": 175.4,
      "duration_seconds": 5.68,
      "text": "Right. Anything else, even from the chemist? Herbal things, painkillers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.27,
      "end_seconds": 187.16,
      "duration_seconds": 8.89,
      "text": "No, just those two. Oh, and I do worry that I forget the vitamin D some days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.21,
      "end_seconds": 196.55,
      "duration_seconds": 8.34,
      "text": "Don't fret about that, a missed day here and there matters very little."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.79,
      "end_seconds": 204.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.83,
      "text": "Okay. Should I be taking something stronger for the tiredness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.36,
      "end_seconds": 219.19,
      "duration_seconds": 12.83,
      "text": "Not yet. There are lots of reasons for tiredness in MS, so I want to look at the whole picture first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.95,
      "end_seconds": 224.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "What sort of reasons?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.67,
      "end_seconds": 237.8,
      "duration_seconds": 10.13,
      "text": "Thyroid levels, vitamin levels, anaemia, poor sleep, low mood. Your thyroid has been underactive for a while, hasn't it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.32,
      "end_seconds": 250.19,
      "duration_seconds": 10.87,
      "text": "Yes, my underactive thyroid, it's been about eight years now. And the MS was diagnosed six years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.25,
      "end_seconds": 258.07,
      "duration_seconds": 6.82,
      "text": "Thank you. Any operations in the past that I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 260.2,
      "end_seconds": 265.32,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "Only my appendix, about fifteen years ago. Nothing since."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.1,
      "end_seconds": 275.34,
      "duration_seconds": 9.24,
      "text": "Okay. And just so I have it right for your record, do you have any allergies to medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.43,
      "end_seconds": 284.08,
      "duration_seconds": 7.65,
      "text": "No, none that I know of. I've never had a reaction to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.65,
      "end_seconds": 295.31,
      "duration_seconds": 8.66,
      "text": "Lovely. Let's get your observations done now. Sam will help with the scales first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 296.09,
      "end_seconds": 303.62,
      "duration_seconds": 7.53,
      "text": "Hello, Priya. Could you step onto the scales for me, shoes off, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 304.88,
      "end_seconds": 311.24,
      "duration_seconds": 6.36,
      "text": "Of course. Oh dear, I hope it hasn't gone up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 320.27,
      "end_seconds": 329.43,
      "duration_seconds": 9.16,
      "text": "It's fine, don't worry. Back to the chair when you're ready, and the doctor will take the rest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 345.74,
      "end_seconds": 353.43,
      "duration_seconds": 7.69,
      "text": "Your blood pressure is 118 over 76, and your pulse is 68 and regular."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 355.46,
      "end_seconds": 363.25,
      "duration_seconds": 7.79,
      "text": "Is that good? It sounded a bit fast when I counted at home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 374.15,
      "end_seconds": 382.1,
      "duration_seconds": 7.95,
      "text": "That's a perfectly comfortable pulse. Temperature is 36.7 degrees, and oxygen saturation is 98 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 383.58,
      "end_seconds": 392.21,
      "duration_seconds": 8.63,
      "text": "And the weight I took was 64 kilograms. Same as last time, I believe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 394.67,
      "end_seconds": 401.28,
      "duration_seconds": 6.61,
      "text": "Yes, that matches. So no big changes, which is reassuring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 402.31,
      "end_seconds": 412.46,
      "duration_seconds": 10.15,
      "text": "So what happens now? I really don't want to just go home and carry on feeling like this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 414.79,
      "end_seconds": 423.64,
      "duration_seconds": 8.85,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a blood test today, covering your thyroid function, vitamin D, iron and blood count."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 424.48,
      "end_seconds": 429.91,
      "duration_seconds": 5.43,
      "text": "And if those are all normal? I'd be so frustrated."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 431.59,
      "end_seconds": 441.61,
      "duration_seconds": 10.02,
      "text": "Then we look at sleep, mood and pacing your day. Fatigue is real, and we'd treat it as real."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 442.92,
      "end_seconds": 450.1,
      "duration_seconds": 7.18,
      "text": "That helps to hear. I sometimes feel everyone thinks I'm just lazy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 450.88,
      "end_seconds": 459.16,
      "duration_seconds": 8.28,
      "text": "Nobody here does. I'll ring you with the results, and we can talk through next steps together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 461.37,
      "end_seconds": 474.92,
      "duration_seconds": 13.55,
      "text": "Priya, pop by my desk afterwards and I'll hand you the blood form and show you the way to the phlebotomy room."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 477.86,
      "end_seconds": 485.45,
      "duration_seconds": 7.59,
      "text": "Will do. Thank you, doctor, I feel a little less panicky than when I walked in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 487.02,
      "end_seconds": 491.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Good. Be kind to yourself, Priya."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 492.48,
      "end_seconds": 495.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "I'll try. Bye for now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 497.72,
      "end_seconds": 498.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Goodbye."
    }
  ]
}
